# In C:
# x=getchar();
# if(x == 5){
# y = 3;
# print(y)
# }

# So if you input '5' it should return 3 which is the value of y. If you input another value, it will output nothing.

# x = getchar()
LISTEN


# Copy x from c0 into c2 and c3, clearing c0
PARK
  RIGHT RIGHT GAS RIGHT GAS LEFT LEFT LEFT BRAKE
DRIVE

# Move c3 back into c0
RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT
PARK
  GEAR 3 LEFT GAS GEAR 3 RIGHT BRAKE
DRIVE

# Set c4 = 1
RIGHT GAS

# If c2 == 53 ('5' as typed input), this leaves the right cells in the expected state
LEFT LEFT
PARK
  GEAR 53 BRAKE
  PARK
    RIGHT
  DRIVE
  RIGHT RIGHT
  PARK
    GEAR 3 LEFT GEAR 51 GAS HONK  # set y cell to ASCII 51 ('3') and print it
    GEAR 3 RIGHT
    PARK
      BRAKE
    DRIVE
  DRIVE
DRIVE

RIGHT GEAR 10 GAS HONK